<title>USA: Stone &amp; Webster gets $40 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Stone &amp; Webster gets $40 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stone &amp; Webster Inc said it has been awarded a contract to engineer, design, procure and construct a geothermal plant for Amoseas Indonesia Inc.</p>
<p>The total project is worth about $109 million. Stone &amp; Webster, which is part of an international consortium working on the project, said its part is worth about $40 million.</p>
<p>Work has begun on the engineering and design phases of a second unit of the Darajat geothermal station, the company said.</p>
<p>The other participants in the consortium are Hyundai Engineering Co, a Korean construction company, and Kanematsu Corp, a Japanese trading house.</p>
